WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
The framework categorizes language pairs into document-rich teacher languages...

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.980
...and document-poor student languages.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.140
Training begins with multilingual sentence-level neural machine translation, or SenNMT...

4
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.290
...which is finetuned into a multilingual document-level translation model, DocNMT.

5
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.560
In the initial SenNMT stage, document-rich languages are pretrained using parallel sentence pairs...

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.600
...jointly with sentence pairs from document-poor languages.

7
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:28.600
For DocNMT, teacher languages are trained on full document pairs to capture cross-sentence contextual modeling.

8
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:36.090
Finally, zero-shot transfer empowers student languages to translate documents in context without ever seeing parallel document pairs during training.

